		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Swinging Pendulum Demo]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=1595#p1595"><![CDATA[
I created a demo of a sphere dangling from a grid of planes tied together by hinge constraints.  If you hit spacebar a force will be applied to the sphere.  Hit "F" to fire a bullet which will break the grid of planes and cause the ball and partial chain to fall to the ground.<br><br>For some reason, the hinge constraint only works in Blender 2.42.  My compiled version of the new physics engine (1.9, i think) causes really weird behaviour.  It could just be the way I compiled it, though.<br><br>Divx AVI:<br><a href="http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.avi" class="postlink">http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.avi</a><br><br>Zip and blend file:<br><a href="http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.zip" class="postlink">http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.zip</a><br><a href="http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.blend" class="postlink">http://www.feltstone.com/BulletPendulum.blend</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=657">feltstone</a> — Fri Aug 25, 2006 9:09 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
